## Provider Failure Safety Tests

The new [provider-failure-safety.test.ts](file:///c:/Users/PC-store/Documents/Projets/Nodiox/apps/auth/src/__tests__/api/provider-failure-safety.test.ts) covers:

| Simulation | Routes Tested | Assertion |
|------------|---------------|-----------|
| `redis-down` | `/login`, `/send-otp` | 429 with `"Too many attempts..."`, no Redis internals |
| `supabase-down` | `/login`, `/send-otp` | 500 with `"An unexpected error occurred"`, no DB URL/email |
| `notification-down` | `/login`, `/send-otp` | 500 with `"An unexpected error occurred"`, no API key/email |
| Header containment | `/login` (all 3) | Simulation header values never echoed in response body |

Every test runs 14 leak-detection regex patterns against the raw response body to catch:
- Postgres connection strings
- Provider URLs (Supabase, Upstash, Resend, Infobip)
- API keys and service role keys
- JWTs
- Email addresses
- Phone numbers
- Connection error strings (ETIMEDOUT, ECONNREFUSED)

